Chapter: CpuidAvx
  cites Foreword chapter Console

Section: Body

 codex-vm on an AVX host exposes XSAVE and AVX (COMPILER-77 stage 2), so this
 pins the host. The boot admits AVX (stage 3): codex-vm answers OSXSAVE and the
 leaf 0Dh size from this processor's live CR4 and XCR0, so osxsave 1 and 832
 are the guest's own CR4 write and XSETBV of 7, observed from outside.

  bit : Integer, Integer -> Text
  bit (v) (n) = show (bit-and (bit-shru v n) 1)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let one = cpu-cpuid-ecx 1
    in act
      print-line-uni ("max-leaf " & show (cpu-cpuid-eax 0))
      print-line-uni ("xsave " & bit one 26 & " osxsave " & bit one 27 & " avx " & bit one 28)
      print-line-uni ("leaf-d " & show (cpu-cpuid-eax 13) & " " & show (cpu-cpuid-ebx 13) & " " & show (cpu-cpuid-ecx 13))
      print-line-uni ("admitted " & show (peek-qword 36384 0))
    end
  end
